From 1fa54014b0ae42417588f218cd006ea94eb92e4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:08:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app,ui): a stock copy carries its source's
 reduced-fidelity flag; a fidelity refusal silences the sim; the colours read
 the tightened tolerance

- SetStock, UpdateModel's propagation, CreateSetup's clone and
  DeleteSetup's undo carry the chord error on the FromModel stock
  itself; the project saves and loads it on the stock row, and a stock
  from an older file adopts its source's flag on load. Deleting or
  renaming the source no longer stops the laws tightening.
- model_fidelity::program_tol: the program sim and the eye judge at
  the gate's refusal when an op is refused for its model's fidelity,
  so the named refusal is never joined by a gouge line off the same
  material.
- FieldView carries the verdict tolerance its colours are gated at;
  machined_classes and the GPU/CPU eyes read it instead of DEV_TOL.

Projects saved before #911 are left open on the issue (a file-format
decision); see docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-flag-gaps.md.

Refs #1056

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
